# Goal 11: Export __fpclassifyd/__signbitd and __fpclassifyf/__signbitf

## Functions
`__fpclassifyd`, `__signbitd`, `__fpclassifyf`, `__signbitf`

## C Source
- /home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/libm/mathd/internal/fpclassifyd.c
- /home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/libm/mathd/internal/signbitd.c
- /home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/libm/mathf/internal/fpclassifyf.c
- /home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/libm/mathf/internal/signbitf.c

## Rust Source
/home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/newexp/rust-s2/src/lib.rs — lines 117-118, 198-199

## Problem
The test harness calls these functions by their internal names (`__fpclassifyd`,
`__signbitd`) but the Rust binary exports them as `__fpclassify` and `__signbit`.
The test expects both naming conventions to be available.

Currently exported:
- `__fpclassify` (double) — line 117
- `__signbit` (double) — line 118
- `__fpclassifyf` (float) — line 198
- `__signbitf` (float) — line 199

Missing exports:
- `__fpclassifyd` (alias for __fpclassify)
- `__signbitd` (alias for __signbit)

Note: `__fpclassifyf` and `__signbitf` are already exported with the correct
names, but are currently hidden by the crash (Goal 1). Once the crash is fixed,
verify these work.

## What Needs to Change
Add `#[no_mangle]` aliases in lib.rs:
```rust
#[no_mangle] pub extern "C" fn __fpclassifyd(x: f64) -> i32 { mathd::__fpclassifyd(x) }
#[no_mangle] pub extern "C" fn __signbitd(x: f64) -> i32 { mathd::__signbitd(x) }
```

## Success Criteria
- `__fpclassifyd` and `__signbitd` callable with correct results
- `__fpclassifyf` and `__signbitf` produce correct results (after crash fix)
- All classification test cases bitwise-exact with C output
